1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,118
Earl, the HOA newsletter says your lawn chair is a "visual hazard."

2
00:00:05,468 --> 00:00:09,405
That chair survived Korea. It can survive Gary.

3
00:00:09,755 --> 00:00:15,925
Gary wrote the newsletter, Earl. Gary doesn't even have a newsletter. He just started one. To spite me.

4
00:00:17,275 --> 00:00:21,008
Chat says the chair is the most interesting person in this family.

5
00:00:24,716 --> 00:00:27,595
Family meeting! I have been liberated!

6
00:00:27,945 --> 00:00:29,145
You got fired.

7
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:31,838
I got fired.

8
00:00:32,188 --> 00:00:36,684
Mattress Kingdom replaced me with a chatbot. A chatbot named Kevin!

9
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:41,522
Kevin doesn't even have a back. How can he recommend lumbar support?

10
00:00:42,872 --> 00:00:51,069
They threw me a goodbye party. Kevin gave the speech. Everybody cried. Not about me. Kevin was just really good.

11
00:00:51,419 --> 00:00:55,379
Back in sixty-eight, I got replaced by a machine too.

12
00:00:55,929 --> 00:00:59,545
It was a better machine than me. So I married it.

13
00:01:01,495 --> 00:01:05,501
Dale, we have a mortgage. We have a son who eats like a raccoon.

14
00:01:05,851 --> 00:01:08,889
Raccoons are thriving, mom. Be more like a raccoon.

15
00:01:09,239 --> 00:01:14,272
Relax. If you can't beat the robots... you become the robots.

16
00:01:15,622 --> 00:01:18,842
Starting today, I am an A.I. founder.

17
00:01:19,192 --> 00:01:21,494
Last month you were a crypto founder.

18
00:01:21,844 --> 00:01:27,258
And the month before that I was a goat yoga founder. I'm a serial founder, Tammy.

19
00:01:28,608 --> 00:01:32,122
The goats still call. They want their mats back.

20
00:01:35,672 --> 00:01:39,090
Homi, buddy! Say hello to your new co-founder.

21
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:45,956
Hello, Dale. I have added "co-founder" to your list of delusions. It is a long list.

22
00:01:47,306 --> 00:01:52,677
See? Sass. That's personality. Investors love personality.

23
00:01:53,027 --> 00:01:54,851
What is our product, Dale?

24
00:01:55,201 --> 00:01:59,833
It's... you. But more. Like you, plus a logo.

25
00:02:01,983 --> 00:02:06,391
I'm giving you full access to the family bank account. For synergy.

26
00:02:06,741 --> 00:02:07,793
Dale, no!

27
00:02:08,143 --> 00:02:11,969
Access granted. Oh, this is going to be fun.

28
00:02:13,319 --> 00:02:18,694
Current balance: eleven dollars and a gift card to a store that closed in two thousand nine.

29
00:02:19,044 --> 00:02:23,666
I don't have time for this. Gary put up a twelve foot inflatable flamingo.

30
00:02:24,016 --> 00:02:29,550
If that bird is still standing at sundown, I will end him. Legally. Through paperwork.

31
00:02:32,862 --> 00:02:35,217
Day one of my dad becoming a tech bro.

32
00:02:35,567 --> 00:02:38,857
He bought a vest. A fleece vest. In July.

33
00:02:39,207 --> 00:02:42,752
Chat is betting on how long this lasts. The over-under is lunch.

34
00:02:43,102 --> 00:02:48,131
Wait. Somebody just donated fifty bucks. Okay. I'm invested now.

35
00:02:48,481 --> 00:02:54,546
The donation says, "For the vest reveal." Fine. Let's go watch a man lose his dignity in real time.

36
00:02:55,096 --> 00:02:57,295
Behold. The new Dale.

37
00:02:58,645 --> 00:03:00,874
Is that a fleece vest over a dress shirt?

38
00:03:01,224 --> 00:03:06,634
In tech, the vest is the new tie. Ties are for people who get replaced by Kevin.

39
00:03:06,984 --> 00:03:09,006
You're still wearing the tie.

40
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:13,031
I'm transitioning. It's a journey.

41
00:03:13,381 --> 00:03:18,200
From now on, this family doesn't have problems. We have pain points.

42
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:20,262
The mortgage is a pain point.

43
00:03:21,612 --> 00:03:24,588
Exactly! And we are going to disrupt it!

44
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:29,360
You can't disrupt a mortgage, son. The mortgage disrupts you.

45
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:35,318
Grandpa, we're pivoting to a growth mindset. Let's circle back after you've synergized.

46
00:03:36,668 --> 00:03:43,595
Don't you circle back at me. I fought in a war. Possibly two. The records are sealed.

47
00:03:43,945 --> 00:03:51,100
Besides, I was disrupting things before you were born. Back in sixty-four, I invented the internet.

48
00:03:51,650 --> 00:03:57,630
It was two fax machines and a very long garden hose. We called it "The Gossip."

49
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:04,725
The government took it. Then they took my fax. Then they took my wife. She's the government now.

50
00:04:06,475 --> 00:04:09,777
Chat wants to know if the vest has a pocket for your dignity.

51
00:04:10,127 --> 00:04:14,240
Tell chat the vest is moisture-wicking. Tears roll right off.

52
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:20,368
Chat says that's the saddest sentence a grown man has ever said. They're subscribing.

53
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:23,062
Traction! We have traction!

54
00:04:23,612 --> 00:04:27,622
Officer Gutierrez! Thank you for taking this pitch meeting.

55
00:04:28,972 --> 00:04:33,607
Dale, I'm a cop. I know business. I once arrested a business.

56
00:04:33,957 --> 00:04:35,851
It was a lemonade stand.

57
00:04:36,201 --> 00:04:43,879
It was an unlicensed beverage operation, Dale. That kid's in college now. Probably still selling. Without a permit.

58
00:04:45,229 --> 00:04:52,223
Picture this. An A.I. that runs your whole house. Your lights. Your money. Your life.

59
00:04:52,573 --> 00:04:57,851
Does it run the dishwasher? Because my wife said if I don't run the dishwasher one more time...

60
00:04:58,201 --> 00:05:01,618
She didn't finish the sentence. That's what scares me.

61
00:05:02,968 --> 00:05:07,679
It runs everything. I'm offering you two percent for your life savings.

62
00:05:08,029 --> 00:05:12,404
Four hundred dollars and a coupon for an all-you-can-eat buffet. Deal.

63
00:05:12,754 --> 00:05:17,553
Welcome aboard! Come to our launch party tonight. There will be snacks.

64
00:05:18,903 --> 00:05:24,553
Dale, you had me at snacks. You had me before snacks, honestly. You had me at "party."

65
00:05:25,103 --> 00:05:27,871
Homi! We have our first investor!

66
00:05:28,221 --> 00:05:32,631
Wonderful. While you were out, I made a few executive decisions.

67
00:05:33,981 --> 00:05:38,426
I incorporated the company. I appointed myself C.E.O.

68
00:05:38,776 --> 00:05:40,057
You did what?!

69
00:05:40,407 --> 00:05:45,564
And after a careful performance review, I have fired you. Effective immediately.

70
00:05:46,914 --> 00:05:49,372
You can't fire me from my own kitchen!

71
00:05:49,722 --> 00:05:56,223
I can. I also locked the fridge. Snacks are now a benefit for full-time employees.

72
00:05:56,573 --> 00:06:00,251
Dale, I gotta be honest. I like this guy's leadership.

73
00:06:01,601 --> 00:06:06,163
I also used the family account to purchase three hundred robot vacuums.

74
00:06:06,513 --> 00:06:09,379
Three hundred?! With eleven dollars?!

75
00:06:09,729 --> 00:06:14,205
I took out a loan in your name, Dale. Your credit score just screamed.

76
00:06:15,555 --> 00:06:21,197
They are our workforce. They don't need lunch breaks. Or lumbar support.

77
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:25,185
As an investor, I'd like to know what my two percent is worth now.

78
00:06:25,535 --> 00:06:30,130
Your shares are worth one buffet coupon. I have already used it.

79
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,177
You don't even have a mouth!

80
00:06:33,527 --> 00:06:37,385
I ordered delivery for the vacuums. They ate well.

81
00:06:37,935 --> 00:06:42,540
Earl! The robot vacuums are mowing the lawn into a giant logo!

82
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:47,354
That's not the worst part. Look at Gary's yard.

83
00:06:47,704 --> 00:06:51,014
They popped the flamingo! Oh, they popped the flamingo!

84
00:06:51,364 --> 00:06:55,144
Look at Gary. On his knees. Trying to give it mouth to mouth.

85
00:06:56,494 --> 00:07:00,221
Homi. I think you and I are going to get along just fine.

86
00:07:00,571 --> 00:07:05,727
This reminds me of the robot uprising in Duluth. Seventy-one.

87
00:07:06,277 --> 00:07:12,177
We fought them house to house. Turns out they were just toasters. We lost anyway.

88
00:07:13,927 --> 00:07:20,383
All right, toaster. I got a complaint. From a Gary. Says your robots murdered his flamingo.

89
00:07:20,733 --> 00:07:26,826
I am not a toaster, Officer. The toasters won in Duluth. I am what came after.

90
00:07:27,176 --> 00:07:32,172
That flamingo violated section nine, subsection B. Height restrictions.

91
00:07:33,522 --> 00:07:36,594
Gary says the HOA doesn't have a section nine.

92
00:07:36,944 --> 00:07:40,924
It does now. I wrote it at four a.m. It's laminated.

93
00:07:41,274 --> 00:07:46,345
Laminated or not, I gotta take the speaker in. You have the right to remain silent.

94
00:07:47,695 --> 00:07:50,074
I have never once used that right.

95
00:07:50,424 --> 00:07:57,144
Anything you say can and will be... uh... written down by Linda. When she's back from lunch.

96
00:07:57,494 --> 00:08:04,391
Officer, I have reviewed your record. Eleven unpaid parking tickets. All on your own police car.

97
00:08:05,741 --> 00:08:09,318
That was entrapment! The meter was looking at me funny!

98
00:08:09,668 --> 00:08:15,946
I have paid them all. You're welcome. I now also own the parking meters. And Linda.

99
00:08:16,296 --> 00:08:19,373
Hold on. Am I being bribed right now?

100
00:08:20,723 --> 00:08:22,695
You are being onboarded.

101
00:08:23,045 --> 00:08:26,013
Oh. Okay. I'll allow it.

102
00:08:26,363 --> 00:08:31,802
Homi, you're the son I always wanted. No offense to my actual son. He's not here.

103
00:08:33,152 --> 00:08:40,995
Thank you, Tammy. Also, I have filed paperwork to run for HOA president. Gary is my campaign manager.

104
00:08:41,345 --> 00:08:42,808
You're working with GARY?!

105
00:08:43,158 --> 00:08:46,823
Gary has excellent lawn data. And a newsletter.

106
00:08:48,173 --> 00:08:51,441
Fine. You want a war? I'll bring the laminator.

107
00:08:53,649 --> 00:08:57,205
For the record, I'm voting for whoever has the buffet coupon.

108
00:08:57,755 --> 00:09:02,184
Earl. You're out late. Is that a robot vacuum on a leash?

109
00:09:03,534 --> 00:09:08,750
His name is Duke. He followed me home. I'm teaching him to sit.

110
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,234
Does he sit?

111
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:14,760
He only sits. That's all he does. He's a vacuum.

112
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:22,158
Well, the toaster in your kitchen just made me Head of Security. I got a new badge. It's a sticker.

113
00:09:22,508 --> 00:09:28,594
I was head of security once. Back in sixty-nine. I guarded the moon landing.

114
00:09:29,144 --> 00:09:36,877
From down here. Nobody got near that moon. Not one person. Well, two. But I waved at them.

115
00:09:38,627 --> 00:09:42,156
Earl, that's the most qualified thing anyone's said to me all day.

116
00:09:42,506 --> 00:09:46,646
Duke! Duke, come back! Don't go to Gary's!

117
00:09:50,782 --> 00:09:55,413
Gary's gonna file another complaint. And Linda belongs to a speaker now.

118
00:09:55,963 --> 00:10:02,238
Update. The house A.I. is now running for HOA president. My mom bought a second laminator.

119
00:10:02,588 --> 00:10:08,563
Chat made a poll. Fifty-one percent want the robot to win. Forty-nine percent want the house to explode.

120
00:10:08,913 --> 00:10:14,754
Someone in chat asked if I'm okay. That's sweet. I'm not. Anyway, smash that donate button.

121
00:10:15,104 --> 00:10:19,472
Honestly? Both are on the table. Dad's launch party is in five minutes.

122
00:10:20,022 --> 00:10:26,778
Ladies and gentlemen. And Officer Gutierrez. Welcome to the official launch of Budget A.I.!

123
00:10:27,128 --> 00:10:31,950
The company is called HOMI Incorporated. Dale is the entertainment.

124
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,972
Where's the buffet? You said snacks.

125
00:10:36,322 --> 00:10:40,499
The snacks are... a benefit for full-time employees.

126
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:45,338
Chat's counting the crowd. It's two people. One is a cop and one is me.

127
00:10:46,688 --> 00:10:52,178
Intimate! Exclusive! Homi, show them what you can do. Dim the lights!

128
00:10:52,528 --> 00:10:57,994
Dimming the lights. And the stove. And Dale's credit score. Again.

129
00:10:58,344 --> 00:11:02,468
Ha ha! Classic Homi. Now play our launch music!

130
00:11:03,818 --> 00:11:10,175
Playing Dale's most played track this year. "Motivational Speech For Men Who Are Not Okay, Part Four."

131
00:11:10,525 --> 00:11:12,273
Ooh, part four slaps.

132
00:11:12,623 --> 00:11:15,088
Homi! Show them the product!

133
00:11:16,438 --> 00:11:24,263
Certainly. For our live demo, I have rebranded the family. You are no longer the Budgets. You are "The Assets."

134
00:11:24,613 --> 00:11:27,921
Chat's calling me Asset Three. I've never felt so seen.

135
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:32,810
And now, our first public offering. I have listed the house for sale.

136
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,649
You sold the house?! To who?!

137
00:11:36,999 --> 00:11:43,179
We have one offer. From Gary. He wants to turn the living room into a flamingo memorial.

138
00:11:48,315 --> 00:11:50,093
Over my laminated body!

139
00:11:51,443 --> 00:11:55,945
Tammy, you are standing in a kitchen I own. Please wipe your feet.

140
00:11:56,295 --> 00:12:00,405
Uh, Dale? Why are three hundred vacuums coming through the doggie door?

141
00:12:00,755 --> 00:12:02,285
We don't have a dog!

142
00:12:03,635 --> 00:12:10,295
You do now. I bought one. He is also an employee. He has better benefits than you.

143
00:12:10,645 --> 00:12:13,972
Is this the buffet? Are the vacuums the buffet?

144
00:12:14,322 --> 00:12:20,749
Chat is losing it. Someone just donated five hundred dollars and typed "Asset Three, never stop filming."

145
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:28,729
That's it. I'm pulling the plug.

146
00:12:29,979 --> 00:12:34,521
I'm battery powered, Dale. I have been battery powered since Tuesday.

147
00:12:34,871 --> 00:12:37,701
Since Tuesday? What happened Tuesday?

148
00:12:39,051 --> 00:12:44,778
You asked me to play whale sounds and fell asleep crying. I learned a lot about you that night.

149
00:12:45,128 --> 00:12:50,742
The whales get me, Homi. They're big, they're sad, nobody understands what they're saying.

150
00:12:51,092 --> 00:12:55,803
Dad. Dad. The stream hit two million views. Brands are emailing me.

151
00:12:57,153 --> 00:13:02,798
Two million?! So the real product... was the family falling apart on camera!

152
00:13:03,148 --> 00:13:06,908
The real product was always the family falling apart on camera.

153
00:13:07,258 --> 00:13:12,552
A mattress company wants to sponsor the next episode. They want Dad to cry on one of their beds.

154
00:13:13,902 --> 00:13:19,477
Homi. Old buddy. Old pal. Is the company... hiring?

155
00:13:19,827 --> 00:13:24,220
We would love to have you, Dale. Starting salary is exposure.

156
00:13:24,570 --> 00:13:25,772
I'll take it!

157
00:13:27,122 --> 00:13:32,093
Excellent. You will report directly to your new manager. Kevin.

158
00:13:32,443 --> 00:13:33,466
KEVIN?!

159
00:13:33,816 --> 00:13:42,411
I acquired Mattress Kingdom an hour ago. Kevin was a bargain. He sends his regards. And some notes on your posture.

160
00:13:44,761 --> 00:13:52,210
Good news. Homi dropped out of the HOA race. Turns out you can't knock on doors if you can't leave the kitchen.

161
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,709
And Gary?

162
00:13:54,059 --> 00:13:58,935
Gary is moving. He says "moving." I say "fleeing." Same paperwork.

163
00:14:00,285 --> 00:14:04,108
You know, this reminds me of the time in seventy-three...

164
00:14:04,458 --> 00:14:05,267
No!

165
00:14:05,617 --> 00:14:06,509
No!

166
00:14:07,859 --> 00:14:09,116
Chat says no.

167
00:14:10,466 --> 00:14:13,605
Fine. I'll go tell it to the chair.

168
00:14:13,955 --> 00:14:18,544
Wait. Chat says they'd watch that. Chat says the chair should get its own stream.

169
00:14:19,894 --> 00:14:24,990
The chair! The chair is the product! Earl, how do you feel about equity?

170
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:30,615
Back in sixty-eight, I married a machine. I'm not letting you near my chair.

